---
permalink: /comments-posts.json
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Every post that currently exists, and nothing else.

    The comments worker fetches this once a week and deletes the stored
    comments of any post that has dropped off it — after a 30-day grace
    period and a warning email, because a renamed post looks exactly like a
    deleted one from the other end.

    Deliberately its own file rather than a read of search.json: that one
    carries the full text of every post (wasteful to fetch weekly) and its
    shape belongs to the search feature. This is a contract with the worker,
    so it should be free to stay this boring.

    These paths are NOT run through HtmlBasePlugin — it only rewrites href
    and src in HTML — so they match the data-post attribute the widget
    sends, which is the same raw page.url. Keep it that way. -#}
[
{%- for post in collections.posts %}
  {{ post.url | dump | safe }}{{ "," if not loop.last }}
{%- endfor %}
]
